<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent liftings fall in week to Oct 8.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent liftings fall in week to Oct 8.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loadings of Brent crude from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal rell to 691,242 tonnes in the week to October 8, down from 801,742 tonnes the previous week, the Shetland Islands Council Marine Operations Department said.</p>
<p>All but one of the cargoes were destined for refineries in NWE Europe. One cargo of 138,613 tonnes went to Philadelphia compared with 248,252 tonnes to U.S. desinations last week.</p>
<p>Below is a list of loadings:</p>
